File: png.c
Line: 2628
Function: png_ascii_from_fixed
Bug type: integer-overflow
CWE: CWE-190
Explanation: Negating a 32-bit signed minimum value is undefined behavior: when fp == INT_MIN (-2147483648), the expression -fp overflows a signed int before being cast to png_uint_32. This UB can lead to miscompilation and unpredictable behavior. The safe approach is to convert to unsigned before negation or handle INT_MIN explicitly.

